From 17f1d70d2bac0a4b772c6020220d45105a82c1ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:34:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] dist: room for the ESP past the ISO

%.iso appends 2 MB to the ISO image and puts the ESP into the last
whole cylinder of fdisk's geometry ('a p1 $-1 $'). A cylinder can be
larger than 2 MB (heads*sectors*512 bytes, up to 255*63*512 = 7.8 MB;
4 MB for a 1.5 GB image), so the cylinder could begin inside the ISO
and disk/format wrote the FAT over the end of it, where mk9660 puts
the Joliet tree (xorriso: "recorded in interleaved mode"). Append
16 MB: two whole cylinders of any geometry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/lib/dist/mkfile | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/lib/dist/mkfile b/sys/lib/dist/mkfile
index 125435aed..c3133442c 100644
--- a/sys/lib/dist/mkfile
+++ b/sys/lib/dist/mkfile
@@ -153,7 +153,10 @@ cd:V:	/tmp/9front.386.iso.gz
 		-p <{cat $proto $bootproto} \
 		-s /n/src9 -v 'Plan 9 Front ('^$objtype^')' $target
 	if(test -r /n/src9/386/9boothyb){
-		dd -if /dev/zero -bs 2048 -count 1024 >> $target
+		# the ESP is the last whole cylinder ($-1 $); keep two
+		# cylinders of any fdisk geometry (at most 255*63*512 bytes)
+		# past the ISO, so it does not begin inside it
+		dd -if /dev/zero -bs 2048 -count 8192 >> $target
 		disk/partfs -m /n/partfs $target
 		disk=/n/partfs/sdXX
 		disk/mbr -m /n/src9/386/mbr $disk/data
